{
  "dom_id": "step-e4015",
  "name": "Example: Combining Logarithms With Coefficients Using the Product Rule",
  "problem": "Express $3\\log_{5}{7}+3\\log_{5}{3}$ as a single logarithm.",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the product rule for logarithms:\n\n$$\n\\log_n a + \\log_n b = \\log_n(ab)\n$$\n\nIf we factor the given expression and use the product rule for logarithms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{log}_{5}⁡7+3{log}_{5}⁡3 & =3({log}_{5}⁡7+{log}_{5}⁡3) \\\\  & =3{log}_{5}⁡(7\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =3{log}_{5}⁡21.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n3\\log_{5}{7}+3\\log_{5}{3} = 3\\log_{5} 21 .\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
